NAME
    xxd, hexdump - display a hexadecimal and ASCII dump

SYNOPSIS
    xxd [path]
    hexdump [path]

DESCRIPTION
    Prints a hexadecimal and ASCII byte dump in the same layout used by
    mem(1). When [path] is given (and no stdin is piped), reads raw
    bytes directly from the file inside the shell sandbox without text
    decoding. When piped standard input is present, dumps its UTF-8
    encoded bytes.

    'hexdump' is an alias for xxd.

EXAMPLES
    dump WRAM 0 256 wram.bin
    xxd /Logs/SNES/wram.bin
    echo hi | xxd

EXIT STATUS
    0   Hexdump printed (or empty output for 0 bytes).
    1   No path and no piped stdin, path outside sandbox, file not
        found, or read error.

SEE ALSO
    mem(1), dump(1), cat(1)
